course: dictionary
lesson: 13579
title: Incinerate: burning until only ash is left
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incinerate is a big word, but the sentence often gives you clues. «The plant incinerates old rubbish, and only grey ash is left.» The clues are old rubbish and grey ash, so incinerate must mean to burn something completely until only ashes are left.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «The plant burns old rubbish completely, and only grey ash is left.» It still makes sense, so burn is the right idea. Incinerate is the stronger, more formal word.
explain: Sometimes the word is used in a story. «The laser incinerated the alien ship in one flash.» Nobody is burning rubbish here. The clue is the laser, which is so hot that the ship is destroyed completely. Here incinerate means to destroy with great heat.
fact: Incinerate means to burn something completely until only ashes are left.
fact: Rubbish and waste are often incinerated, and some incinerators make electricity.
fact: Hospitals incinerate used medical waste to get rid of it safely.
fact: In stories, «incinerate» can mean to destroy completely with great heat, such as a laser.
fact: Incinerate is a verb: incinerate, incinerates, incinerated, incinerating.
exercise: «The factory incinerates its waste, so only ash is left.» What does incinerates mean? | Freezes solid | Recycles into new paper | *Burns completely until only ashes are left | Buries under the ground
exercise: «In the story, the laser incinerated the alien ship in a flash.» What does incinerated mean here? | Painted bright blue | *Destroyed completely with great heat | Hidden in a cave | Carefully taken apart piece by piece
exercise: Hospitals must ___ used medical waste safely. Which word fits best? | admire | stretch | whistle | *incinerate
test: «The old rubbish was incinerated at the plant, leaving only grey ash.» What does incinerated mean? | Sold to a shop | *Burned completely until only ashes were left | Sorted into piles | Stored in a warm room
test: Some rubbish cannot be recycled, so the council sends it to be burned. Which word means burn it completely until only ash is left? | *Incinerates | Sweeps | Dampens | Admires
exam: Which sentence uses incinerate correctly? | The children incinerated their sandwiches and laughed at the sun. | *The plant incinerates waste that cannot be recycled, leaving only ash. | Ella incinerated her homework on the bus to school. | The dog incinerated its bone happily in the park.
